From: conda-forge nmma feedstock
Subject: [PATCH] Require `tensorflow` instead of `tensorflow-cpu` in metadata

On conda-forge the CPU TensorFlow build is provided by `tensorflow-base`,
whose Python distribution is named `tensorflow` (there is no `tensorflow-cpu`
dist-info). The recipe still depends on the `tensorflow-cpu` conda package to
get the CPU build, but the installed distribution reports itself as
`tensorflow`, so an unpatched `tensorflow-cpu` requirement makes `pip check`
fail. Rewrite the metadata requirement to `tensorflow` to match; the upstream
PyPI package keeps `tensorflow-cpu` to avoid pulling CUDA wheels.

--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -49,5 +49,5 @@
     "ligo.skymap",
     "healpy",
     "scikit-learn",
-    'tensorflow-cpu>=2.19; platform_system == "Linux"',
+    'tensorflow>=2.19; platform_system == "Linux"',
 ]
